  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c089c74a-89b3-4bf2-bb9a-8f5d45c379b1",
    "name": "Mono Connect API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "A grounded subset of the Mono open banking API for Africa. Mono lets businesses link customer bank accounts and read financial data, assess creditworthiness, collect direct bank payments (DirectPay), and verify identity (Lookup). Server-to-server requests authenticate with a secret key sent in the `mono-sec-key` header. Account linking is completed by the customer through the hosted Mono Connect widget; the widget returns a short-lived authorization code that is exchanged for a permanent account id used on all financial-data calls.\n\nEndpoint paths and methods here are grounded in the public Mono documentation at docs.mono.co (base host `https://api.withmono.com`, most endpoints under `/v2`; the account-number and Mashup Lookup endpoints are under `/v3`). Request and response bodies are modeled representatively - treat field-level schemas as illustrative and confirm exact payloads against the live reference before relying on them.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Mono",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
